{"name":"Meerkat","hex":"#ab7647","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"meerkat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Suricata suricatta, a small carnivorous mammal of the mongoose family, from the Kalahari Desert, known for its habit of standing on its hind legs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meerkat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Meerkat","blocks":[{"text":"The meerkat or suricate is a small mongoose found in southern Africa. It is characterised by a broad head, large eyes, a pointed snout, long legs, a thin tapering tail, and a brindled coat pattern. The head-and-body length is around 24–35 cm (9.4–13.8 in), and the weight is typically between 0.62 and 0.97 kg. The coat is light grey to yellowish-brown with alternate, poorly defined light and dark bands on the back. Meerkats have foreclaws adapted for digging and have the ability to thermoregulate to survive in their harsh, dry habitat. Three subspecies are recognised."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Meerkat_%28Suricata_suricatta%29_Tswalu.jpg/330px-Meerkat_%28Suricata_suricatta%29_Tswalu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meerkat","wikidata":"Q134015"},{"title":"MeerKAT","blocks":[{"text":"MeerKAT, originally the Karoo Array Telescope, is a radio telescope consisting of 64 antennas in the Meerkat National Park, in the Northern Cape of South Africa. In 2003, South Africa submitted an expression of interest to host the Square Kilometre Array (SKA) Radio Telescope in Africa, and the locally designed and built MeerKAT was incorporated into the first phase of the SKA. MeerKAT was launched in 2018. MeerKAT is located inside a radio quiet zone within the park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/2018-MeerKAT-1.png/330px-2018-MeerKAT-1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MeerKAT","wikidata":"Q6807657"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Meerkat_area.png/250px-Meerkat_area.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Meerkat_area.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Meerkat_area.png/250px-Meerkat_area.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMeerkat_area.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/112_Meerkat_standing_in_the_Kalahari_Desert_of_Namibia_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/500px-112_Meerkat_standing_in_the_Kalahari_Desert_of_Namibia_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/112_Meerkat_standing_in_the_Kalahari_Desert_of_Namibia_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/1280px-112_Meerkat_standing_in_the_Kalahari_Desert_of_Namibia_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/112_Meerkat_standing_in_the_Kalahari_Desert_of_Namibia_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/500px-112_Meerkat_standing_in_the_Kalahari_Desert_of_Namibia_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Meerkat standing in the Kalahari desert of Namibia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A112_Meerkat_standing_in_the_Kalahari_Desert_of_Namibia_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Suricata_suricatta_%28Meerkats%29%2C_Gordon_drawing.jpg/500px-Suricata_suricatta_%28Meerkats%29%2C_Gordon_drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, h